From 7481fed985a5864f10a9b6fbfb26748dd010b7cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: askimi <44218719+RNI4114@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:43:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] jay: turn chains of 8-bit dot products against constant
 weights into DPAS

Per-pixel networks (FSR4's INT8 model through vkd3d-proton) compute
acc[c] += dot4(x[k], W[c][k]) with W as immediates. Across a SIMD16
subgroup that is an int8 DPAS with the invocations' x as B and the
results landing where acc already is; only the weights move, to the
shader's constant data, read as A by a subgroup block read.

Shaders are pinned to SIMD16 unless they require another subgroup size
and can observe it. Non-uniform blocks are handled when not in a loop
and every non-uniform if around them has an empty other side (bounds
checks), since DPAS writes all lanes. Bit exact; INTEL_DOT4_DPAS=0
turns it off. On FSR4 4.1.1 INT8, 7 of the 14 dot product shaders (the
heavy ones) go from SIMD32 with spills to SIMD16 without dp4a or spills.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
